      <div id="help" class="overlay">
        <div class="overlay-card help-card">
          <h2 id="help-title">How to play</h2>
          <div class="help-grid">
            <div><b>Tap mana</b><p>${ni("Click","Tap")} your lands and mana rocks in a main phase to add mana to your pool (glowing cards pay for themselves).</p></div>
            <div><b>Cast spells</b><p>${ni("Click a card in your hand, or drag a glowing card onto the table.","Tap a card in your hand, or drag a glowing card onto the table.")} ${ni("Hold <b>Alt</b> or right-click to inspect.","Long-press to inspect, then release to close.")} You can only cast it if you have enough mana (the badge shows the cost).</p></div>
            <div><b>Play a land</b><p>${ni("Click","Tap")} a land in hand to put it onto the battlefield (one per turn).</p></div>
            <div><b>Attack</b><p>The gold button offers a sensible attack (<b>Attack with 2</b>, the ⚔ creatures) — press it, or ${ni("click","tap")} your creatures to choose your own (from your first main phase too), then <b>Attack with N</b>. <b>Skip combat</b> keeps them home. ${ni("Click","Tap")} an attacker again to take it back; with several players (or a planeswalker) each ${ni("click","tap")} first sends it at the next one, and its chip names its target. Blocking works the same way: ${ni("click","tap")} your creature to block the next attacker it can.${ni(" <b>Shift+click</b> attacks the same player as last time.","")}</p></div>
            <div><b>Block</b><p>When attacked, ${ni("click","tap")} your creature and then the attacker to block it, or take <b>Suggested blocks</b>. ${ni("Click","Tap")} a blocker twice to remove its block, or select it and ${ni("click","tap")} another attacker to move it. Confirm when done. With nothing able to block, the damage is taken for you.</p></div>
            <div><b>Targeting</b><p>Removal spells ask you to ${ni("click","tap")} a target. ${ni("Press <b>Esc</b> or right-click to cancel.","Tap <b>Cancel</b> to stop.")}</p></div>
            <div><b>Commander</b><p>Cast your commander from its command zone card. Recasting costs {2} more each time.</p></div>
            <div><b>Need a rule?</b><p>${ni("Press <b>R</b> any time for","Open the game menu for")} a full rules reference and keyword glossary.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="help-keys cx-mouse-block help-shortcuts"><button type="button" class="ghost tiny" id="help-shortcuts">Every keyboard shortcut <kbd>?</kbd></button><span><kbd>Space</kbd> does the gold button · <kbd>E</kbd> ends your turn · <kbd>Ctrl+Z</kbd> undoes</span></div>
          <div class="help-keys help-camera" aria-label="3D camera controls">
            <span><b>3D camera</b></span>
            <span class="cx-mouse">Right-drag orbit</span>
            <span class="cx-mouse">Drag empty table, middle-drag or <kbd>Shift</kbd>+drag pan</span>
            <span class="cx-mouse">Wheel zoom to cursor · double-click centres</span>
            <span class="cx-mouse"><kbd>W</kbd><kbd>A</kbd><kbd>S</kbd><kbd>D</kbd> / arrows pan</span>
            <span class="cx-mouse"><kbd>Q</kbd>/<kbd>E</kbd> rotate · <kbd>+</kbd>/<kbd>−</kbd> zoom</span>
            <span class="cx-mouse"><kbd>Shift</kbd> faster · <kbd>Home</kbd> reset</span>
            <span>Touch: drag pan · pinch zoom · twist rotate</span>
            <span>Libraries, graveyards, exile and commanders lie on the table: ${ni("click","tap")} a pile to open it, your commander to cast it · the <b>Zones</b> tab opens the zone panel</span>
          </div>
          <div class="overlay-actions sticky-actions">
            <label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="help-reduced"/> Reduce motion</label>
            <button class="primary" id="help-close">Got it</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
